{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "gr-mo",
  "connector": "も",
  "gloss": "too, also",
  "title": "も — too, also",
  "pattern": "A も … (in place of は, が or を)",
  "explanation": "も means “too” or “also”, and it takes the place of は, が or を: {私|わたし}も{行|い}きます — I’m going too; コーヒーも{飲|の}みます — I’ll have coffee too. With a negative, it’s “not… either”: {私|わたし}も{分|わ}かりません — I don’t know either.",
  "natural": "The everyday way to agree: {私|わたし}も！ — me too! It stacks on top of に and で: {東京|とうきょう}にも{行|い}きたい — I want to go to Tokyo too.",
  "stiff": "Don’t keep the particle it replaces: {私|わたし}はも and コーヒーをも are wrong. (に, で and から stay: にも, でも, からも.)",
